  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 1224959,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1941 - The Secret Conflict: A Commodore 64 SHMUP\n\nDive into the intense aerial combat of \"1941 - The Secret Conflict,\" a thrilling shoot 'em up (SHMUP) for the Commodore 64! Inspired by the classic 1942, this game delivers a modern twist on a beloved formula, crafted in 2014 by Gibranx and featuring a captivating soundtrack by Richard Bayliss of TND.\n\nAssume the role of a daring Allied pilot battling against a mysterious and technologically advanced enemy force during World War II. The narrative hints at a hidden conflict, shrouded in secrecy, as you navigate through beautifully rendered, scrolling landscapes. Expect relentless waves of enemy aircraft, formidable bosses, and challenging level designs. \n\n\"1941 - The Secret Conflict\" boasts tight, responsive controls and a vibrant visual style, characteristic of the SEUCK engine.  Experience the adrenaline rush of solo play or team up with a friend for cooperative two-player action, doubling the fun and the firepower! Prepare for a nostalgic yet fresh take on the classic arcade experience."
    },
